<Base title="AD Set Labs — Hexfield Academy" description="A preview of planned OSCP-style Active Directory lab sets focused on systematic investigation and clear debriefs.">
  <div class="academy-breadcrumb wrap"><a href="/academy/">ACADEMY</a><span>/</span><span>AD SET LABS</span></div>
  <section class="academy-detail-hero wrap ad-detail"><div class="detail-heading"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> PATH 01 / PRACTICE</div><h1>AD Set<br /><em>Labs.</em></h1><p>Enterprise environments should feel like connected systems, not isolated tricks. These planned sets will ask you to map the domain, test assumptions, follow evidence, and explain the route you took.</p><div class="detail-tags"><span>OSCP-STYLE</span><span>ACTIVE DIRECTORY</span><span>SCENARIO LED</span></div><div class="detail-status"><span class="academy-status">IN DEVELOPMENT</span><span>Lab access is not available yet.</span></div></div><div class="ad-map" aria-label="Illustrative network map"><div class="map-grid"></div><span class="map-caption">SCENARIO MAP / CONCEPT PREVIEW</span><div class="map-edge edge-one"></div><div class="map-edge edge-two"></div><div class="map-edge edge-three"></div><div class="map-edge edge-four"></div><div class="map-node map-node-one"><b>01</b><small>ENTRY</small></div><div class="map-node map-node-two"><b>02</b><small>HOST</small></div><div class="map-node map-node-three"><b>03</b><small>IDENTITY</small></div><div class="map-node map-node-four"><b>04</b><small>TRUST</small></div><div class="map-node map-node-five"><b>05</b><small>DOMAIN</small></div><span class="map-bottom">OBSERVE <b>→</b> HYPOTHESIZE <b>→</b> VERIFY</span></div></section>
  <section class="academy-detail-section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="section-kicker">THE LAB FORMAT / 01</div><h2>Practice with a method<span class="title-stop">.</span></h2></div><p>The intended learning design combines a scoped environment with prompts and an explanation of the reasoning behind each stage.</p></div><div class="detail-feature-grid"><div><span>01 / SCOPE</span><h3>A connected scenario</h3><p>Hosts, accounts, and relationships form one coherent enterprise story with clear rules of engagement.</p></div><div><span>02 / INVESTIGATE</span><h3>Evidence first</h3><p>Work from observations and hypotheses instead of guessing a predefined command sequence.</p></div><div><span>03 / DEBRIEF</span><h3>Explain the path</h3><p>Review the decisions, missed signals, and defensive meaning of what you found.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="academy-modules wrap"><div class="academy-modules-intro"><span>PLANNED THEMES / 02</span><h2>A progression, not a pile of boxes.</h2><p>These are design themes for future sets, not currently available lab environments.</p></div><div class="module-list"><div><span>SET CONCEPT / 01</span><h3>Domain Foundations</h3><p>Enumerate the environment, identify principals and groups, and establish the trust boundaries that matter.</p><b>→</b></div><div><span>SET CONCEPT / 02</span><h3>Privilege Paths</h3><p>Connect permissions, delegation, and host context into a defensible investigation path.</p><b>→</b></div><div><span>SET CONCEPT / 03</span><h3>Enterprise Chains</h3><p>Practice reasoning across multiple systems, then document the route and the evidence.</p><b>→</b></div></div></section>
  <section class="academy-end wrap"><div><span>BUILD THE FOUNDATION FIRST</span><h2>Start with the free Active Directory notes.</h2></div><a class="button button-primary" href="/roadmap/#active-directory">Open the AD roadmap <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
  <p class="academy-disclaimer wrap">Hexfield is an independent project and is not affiliated with OffSec. “OSCP-style” describes the intended practice format; these labs are not official exam material.</p>
</Base>
